# Field Assist license signing PRIVATE key (base64 Curve25519 raw representation).
#
# This is a TEMPLATE showing the file's shape. Do not copy it and paste a key in by hand —
# generate the key straight into place instead (see below). The key must NEVER be committed or
# shipped — anyone holding it can mint valid Field Assist licenses.
#
# The matching PUBLIC key is embedded in the app at
# `LicenseService.productionPublicKeyBase64` and IS committed (public keys are safe to ship).
#
# Generate a fresh keypair — it writes `secrets/field-assist-signing-key.txt` with mode 0600,
# refuses to overwrite an existing key, and prints ONLY the public half:
#   ./Scripts/generate-field-license.swift keygen secrets/field-assist-signing-key.txt
# Put the printed `public` value into LicenseService.productionPublicKeyBase64.
#
# A private key is written to a file at generation and is NEVER printed — not into a terminal,
# a chat, or a log. A key that has been printed is a key that must be rotated.
#
# Mint a license code (the script finds this file automatically):
#   ./Scripts/generate-field-license.swift "Acme Refrigeration Ltd" [2027-01-01T00:00:00Z]
#
# Or name the key file explicitly, or pipe it in — `--key-file` takes a PATH, never a key:
#   ./Scripts/generate-field-license.swift "Acme" --key-file secrets/field-assist-signing-key.txt
#   printf '%s' "$SIGNING_KEY" | ./Scripts/generate-field-license.swift "Acme" --key-file -
#
# A key passed as an argument is refused. Arguments are visible in `ps`, written to shell
# history, echoed by CI logs and captured in crash reports.
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored; the key is the sole non-comment, non-empty line.
PUT_YOUR_BASE64_PRIVATE_KEY_HERE
